A||||4||Aero_Fiero||Fuel Delivery on 84' 2.5cyl Coupe||||1||
Z||000000||Aero_Fiero||10-03-2000||01:47 PM||||I seem to be having a fuel delivery problem.  When the ign key is turned, I don't hear the fuel boost pump and it doesn't appear that I'm getting any fuel to the carb.  Just wondered if any of you had experience with the fuel system and might direct me in my trouble shooting efforts.  Any help would be much appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||10-03-2000||01:51 PM||||Never overlook the obvious...clogged fuel filter and/or fuel pump fuse. It's also possible that the wiring to the fuel pump has worked loose.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||10-03-2000||02:06 PM||||Check the things deceler8 mentioned first.<P>The wiring to the fuel pump is routed from behind the firewall heat shield down behind a lower heat shield in front of the catalytic converter.  Check to see if the plug hasn't unplugged itself in behind the upper heat shield.  If it's not these things and your not hearing the pump and seeing a flow of gas from the TBI with the air cleaner off, then I'd say a good guess it would be the fuel pump.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Check other power wiring connections too, I had a twistee connecter come apart on a separate power line and had no fuel pump.  Thinking I had a bad pump, I bought one on the way home with my car on the trailer.<P>Took the heat shield off and said "crapola" when I found the twistee pulled apart.  The previous owner must have had a household electrician as a mechanic.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  Fixed the connection and she fired right up, but eventually replaced my badly hacked engine harness.<P>Good luck<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">             <BR>    <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Aero_Fiero||10-03-2000||02:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Aero_Fiero:<BR><B>I seem to be having a fuel delivery problem.  When the ign key is turned, I don't hear the fuel boost pump and it doesn't appear that I'm getting any fuel to the carb.  Just wondered if any of you had experience with the fuel system and might direct me in my trouble shooting efforts.  Any help would be much appreciated.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I did check the fuse and connections at the relays.  I'll do a fuel flow and check the wiring behind the firewall.  What symtoms do bad fuel relay give?  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||wilburt||10-03-2000||06:40 PM||||There is a fuel pump test connector, usually located next to, and afixed to the fuel pump wiring harness. If you put 12v positive current to this test connection, the fuel pump will run if it's OK. The Haynes Repair Manual can explain this much better. Hope this helps.<p>[This message has been edited by wilburt (edited 10-03-2000).]||||reg||3
